# Multi-vendor SEO references

When designing or naming SEO features (backlinks, competitors, keyword gap, audits), do **not** model the product only on Ahrefs or Semrush.

## Primary reference set (industry)

Treat these as first-class product references:

1. **Moz** — Domain Authority (DA), Page Authority (PA), Link Explorer, Spam Score concepts
2. **Majestic** — Trust Flow / Citation Flow, topical trust, referring domains quality
3. **Ahrefs** — DR/UR, referring domains, broken backlinks, content/link gap patterns
4. **Semrush** — Backlink Gap, Keyword Gap, competitive analysis flows
5. **SE Ranking / Serpstat** — practical SaaS competitor & backlink tooling UX
6. **DataForSEO** — current live data engine (API source of truth in this codebase)

## Product rules

- Prefer **vendor-neutral** UI labels: Referring domains, Broken backlinks, Backlink gap, Keyword gap, Domain rank — not “Ahrefs-only” or “Semrush-only” wording in customer UI.
- When explaining standards to users, mention **several** vendors (e.g. Moz + Majestic + Ahrefs + Semrush), not just one or two.
- Live metrics today come from **DataForSEO** (+ GSC + optional Ahrefs import). Do not claim Moz/Majestic live APIs are connected unless those integrations exist.
- Future multi-source work: design for pluggable providers (Moz / Majestic / Ahrefs API) behind the same UI contracts; avoid hardcoding a single-vendor schema in new features.

## Feature parity checklist

| Capability | Reference vendors |
|------------|-------------------|
| Domain strength | Moz DA, Ahrefs DR, Majestic TF/CF, DataForSEO rank |
| Referring domains | All major vendors |
| Broken backlinks | Ahrefs, Semrush, Moz Link Explorer |
| Backlink / link gap | Semrush Backlink Gap, Ahrefs Link Intersect, Moz |
| Keyword gap | Semrush, Ahrefs Content Gap, SE Ranking |
| Competitor discovery | Semrush, Ahrefs, Moz, SE Ranking |
